/F1 14 Tf .0902 .2118 .3647 rg 40 765 Td (7. Task 7 - Reflection Report) Tj
/F2 9 Tf .15 .15 .15 rg
40 742 Td (1. Major Preprocessing Challenges:) Tj
40 728 Td (Multi-format dates, extreme sentinels, currency scaling, and categorical typos required combined median/mode imputation.) Tj

40 702 Td (2. Preprocessing Step with Greatest Impact:) Tj
40 688 Td (Data Cleaning had the greatest overall impact because all downstream transformations depended on clean non-skewed inputs.) Tj

40 662 Td (3. Residual Problems After Preprocessing:) Tj
40 648 Td (Median/mode imputation may introduce slight artificial density spikes, and PCA projection reduces direct feature interpretability.) Tj

40 622 Td (4. Recommended Machine Learning Algorithm:) Tj
40 608 Td (K-Means Clustering and XGBoost Classifiers are recommended for distance-based customer segmentation and repurchase modeling.) Tj

40 582 Td (5. Additional Preprocessing Before Deployment:) Tj
40 568 Td (Automated schema validation pipelines (Great Expectations), payload clipping, and Population Stability Index (PSI) drift monitoring.) Tj

/F1 10 Tf .0902 .2118 .3647 rg 40 500 Td (End of Submission Report - Student: Rashmin Dudhatra (2025EM1300192)) Tj
